    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n<p><strong>Tier 3 — Prophet / Oracle</strong></p><p><strong>“I know which failure matters.”</strong></p><p>At Tier 3, foresight stops being vague and starts becoming operational. You may not know everything that will happen, but you know which branch is dangerous enough to deserve intervention first.</p><p><strong>Tactical (Character Scale)</strong></p><ul><li>1/Soma Break, before a roll is made, declare a creature, ally, or visible event-thread and grant <strong>Advantage</strong> on one attack roll, check, or attribute check tied to avoiding a meaningful failure</li></ul><p><strong>Strategic (Faction Scale)</strong></p><ul><li>Once per Scenario, after a failed key check, you may identify it as a <strong>foreseen failure</strong> and either:</li><ul><li>reroll the check, taking the new result, <em>or</em></li><li>accept the failure but downgrade one attached narrative consequence by one step</li></ul></ul><p><strong>Cost:</strong> strong foresight creates emotional wear and inevitability-dread. Expect fatigue, dread, or the unsettling feeling that saving one branch made another one brighter instead of dimmer.</p><div data-ft-per-use=\"1\" data-ft-per-use-key=\"prophT3\" style=\"margin-top:0.7rem;padding:0.55rem 0.75rem;border:1px solid #b08acc;border-radius:0.35rem;background:rgba(70,55,95,0.18);\">\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.78rem;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#d4b8e8;margin-bottom:0.25rem\">⟁ Per-Use Ability — <strong>Foreseen Failure</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.86rem;opacity:0.92;line-height:1.4\"><strong>Recovery:</strong> 1/Soma Break &nbsp;·&nbsp; <strong>Action:</strong> Free (before roll) &nbsp;·&nbsp; <strong>Use:</strong> Click this feature on your sheet to invoke.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.82rem;opacity:0.85;margin-top:0.3rem\">Declare a creature/ally/event-thread; grant reroll-lowest on one attack/save/check tied to avoiding meaningful failure.</div>\n</div>",
      "chat": ""
    },
